{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Balak took Balaam to the peak of Peor.</b> From this point they reverted to a third strategy, for they saw that they had no opening to introduce even a trace of blemish, neither in the roots nor in the branches. If so, they were at the height of perfection, and anything that is perfect from every side is all the more a place where the evil eye can hold sway — by means of one blessing his fellow in a loud voice and proclaiming his praise in a resounding voice, so that all the nations would hear and grow envious of them and cast the evil eye upon them, and through this it would be accounted a curse for them. And therefore he took him to the peak of Peor, so that he would widen his mouth without limit and proclaim their merit in a resounding voice."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:52.415227346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}